lesson: 158
title: Ages: in how many years will one be twice or three times as old
level: primary-3
stars: 2
explain: The difference between two ages never changes: every year both people get one year older.
explain: When a mother is twice as old as her son, the difference equals the son's age then. Mother 32, son 8: the difference is 24, so the son will be 24, which is in 24 - 8 = 16 years.
explain: When she is three times as old, the difference is two of the son's ages: 24 ÷ 2 = 12, so the son will be 12, in 12 - 8 = 4 years.
vars: a=name b=name n=1..15 c=3..12 k=2..3 z=1..5
let: F = k * (c + n) - n
need: F - c >= 20
need: F <= 60
answer: n
exercise: {a} is {c} years old, and {a.his} mother is {F}. In how many years will the mother be {k.words} times as old as {a}?
exercise: {b}'s father is {F} years old and {b} is {c}. After how many years will the father's age be {k.words} times {b}'s age?
exercise: {a}'s aunt is {F-c} years older than {a}, who is {c} now. In how many years will the aunt be {k.words} times as old as {a}?
exercise: Now {a} is {c} and {a.his} father is {F}. How many years from now will the father be exactly {k.words} times as old as {a}?
exercise: {b} is {c}, and {b.his} uncle is {F}. In how many years will the uncle's age be {k.words} times {b}'s age?
test: In how many years will a {F}-year-old teacher be {k.words} times as old as a pupil of {c}?
test: {a}'s mother is {F-c} years older than {a}. Today {a} turns {c}. In how many years will the mother be {k.words} times as old as {a}?
test: {b} is {c}, {b.his} older cousin is {c+z}, and {b.his} father is {F}. How many years must pass until the father is {k.words} times as old as {b}?
