exam: It is given that {a} is {c} years of age and that the mother of {a} is {F} years of age. Determine the number of years after which the age of the mother shall be {k.words} times that of {a}.
exam: Whereas the father of {b} is aged {F} years and {b} is aged {c} years, ascertain after how many years the age of the father shall be precisely {k} times the age of {b}.
exam: Ascertain the number of years that must elapse before a person now aged {F} years attains an age {k.words} times that of a child now aged {c} years.
exam: An aunt is presently {F} years of age and her nephew {c} years of age. State in how many years hence the age of the aunt shall equal {k.words} times that of her nephew.
exercise: {a}'s mum is a bit creative with the truth about her age: she says she is {F-10}, but she is really {F}. {a} is {c}. In how many years will she be {k.words} times as old as {a}?
exercise: {b}'s dad says he is "over the hill" at {F}. {b} is {c}. In how many years will the dad be {k.words} times as old as {b}?
